  <title>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">Establishment of Community Resource Centres and Mobile CCCM Teams in Underserved Communities in Sari-pul and Jawzjan Provinces</narrative>
  </title>
  <description>
   <narrative xml:lang="EN">The displacement situation in Afghanistan is one of the most complex and largest in recent history. According to the last IOM analysis of the 34 provinces 12,949 settlements were identified as hosting internally displaced persons (IDPs) and returnees, where 62 per cent of the settlements (8,048) had not received any humanitarian or development assistance in the past six months. This situation is likely to continue to deteriorate due the economic disruption that the country is facing, also affecting humanitarian organizations&#x2019; ability to deliver. Under this grant, IOM seeks to provide support to IDPs, returnees and host communities through access to multisectoral assistance, such as primary health care, water supply, and hygiene promotion.</narrative>
  </description>
